{
  "case_id": "2010-09-520",
  "document_hash": "9b58e24a0c1b28294a1dd62529fccac8680fff82d8a3457a1a0c20c98ea39854",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-09-520",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9b58e24a0c1b28294a1dd62529fccac8680fff82d8a3457a1a0c20c98ea39854",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9b58e24a0c1b-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:03 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-09-520",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9b58e24a0c1b28294a1dd62529fccac8680fff82d8a3457a1a0c20c98ea39854",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9b58e24a0c1b-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: But in light of our AFC case, it seems to me that what you are arguing is that"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-520",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9b58e24a0c1b28294a1dd62529fccac8680fff82d8a3457a1a0c20c98ea39854",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9b58e24a0c1b-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Mr. Phillips, this is what troubles me about -- about your position: You make a viscerally appealing case on the facts of this case, where you say that your clients, the railroads, are being taxed more than competing carriers, truckers and -- and water carriers."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Melissa A. Sherry",
      "case_id": "2010-09-520",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9b58e24a0c1b28294a1dd62529fccac8680fff82d8a3457a1a0c20c98ea39854",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9b58e24a0c1b-0000-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. SHERRY: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The only question that the Court needs to resolve today is whether a non-property tax that's imposed on a rail carrier but from which its competitors are exempt can ever be another tax that discriminates against a rail carrier under subsection (b)(4). The answer is yes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2010-09-520",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9b58e24a0c1b28294a1dd62529fccac8680fff82d8a3457a1a0c20c98ea39854",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9b58e24a0c1b-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. SHERRY: The government's position, first with respect to subsection (c), is that it is a broad grant of jurisdiction to the district courts to adjudicate all violations of subsection (b), and that seems clear from the first sentence in that provision."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-520",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9b58e24a0c1b28294a1dd62529fccac8680fff82d8a3457a1a0c20c98ea39854",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9b58e24a0c1b-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: It doesn't make any -- any sense, you are quite right; but -- but Congress thought it made sense in (1) to (3), so why doesn't it make sense in (4)?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-09-520",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9b58e24a0c1b28294a1dd62529fccac8680fff82d8a3457a1a0c20c98ea39854",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9b58e24a0c1b-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, you are arguing in favor of -- you are arguing in favor of a very idiosyncratic interpretation of the concept of a discriminatory tax, aren't you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2010-09-520",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9b58e24a0c1b28294a1dd62529fccac8680fff82d8a3457a1a0c20c98ea39854",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9b58e24a0c1b-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What is the choice?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "CSX",
      "case_id": "2010-09-520",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9b58e24a0c1b28294a1dd62529fccac8680fff82d8a3457a1a0c20c98ea39854",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9b58e24a0c1b-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CSX argues on page 8 and 9 of the reply brief that with regard to property taxes (b)(4) would apply if the tax singles out the railroads. But now they are arguing another tax that discriminates, the very same phrase means any differential treatment of any kind when it comes to non-property taxes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-09-520",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9b58e24a0c1b28294a1dd62529fccac8680fff82d8a3457a1a0c20c98ea39854",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9b58e24a0c1b-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What -- what authority do you have for the proposition that the clear statement rule applies to the exercise of the congressional power under the Commerce Clause? Is that -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-09-520",
      "confidence": 0.97,
      "document_hash": "9b58e24a0c1b28294a1dd62529fccac8680fff82d8a3457a1a0c20c98ea39854",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9b58e24a0c1b-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So give me a definition of discriminate. Give me your working -- it can't -- as I started to ask your adversary, it can't be most favored taxpayer status. True?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Phillips",
      "case_id": "2010-09-520",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "9b58e24a0c1b28294a1dd62529fccac8680fff82d8a3457a1a0c20c98ea39854",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9b58e24a0c1b-0003-0002",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "intended to allow to you favor direct competitors of the railroads when the ultimate effect of that may be to undermine the -- the financial stability of the railroads."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2010-09-520",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "9b58e24a0c1b28294a1dd62529fccac8680fff82d8a3457a1a0c20c98ea39854",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9b58e24a0c1b-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, Mr. Phillips, counsel. Case is submitted."
    },
